2020: "Toon Blast" earns almost $1 billion.

2017: Peak Games buys the company for $100 million.

May 2012: Partnership agreement with Peak Games, rebranding of the company to "Peak Casual";

March 2012: Lost Bubble tops Facebook's top grossing list for 3 weeks, surpassed Candy Crush Saga to become the world's most playable casual game, earning $24 million in its first 24 months.

December 2011: Filling lawsuit with King.com on over £1 million in intellectual property, 
creating "Lost Bubble" and "Lost Jewels" in early 2012;

November 2011: The first "Sultan Bubble" game on Facebook grew to 1 million DAU in 2 weeks, to 5 million DAU in 4 weeks.

September 2011: Reached the conclusion to initiate development of casual games;

2010: Published the first 3 games and won the first 3 places in the Ovi Store in a Nokia competition.

2001-2010: Head of an outsourcing company with 500 completed projects, including cooperation with BridgeStone and Symantec Europe;


