Please write the key mitigation on "the land owner or the lessor of SISBKK’s land does not agree to give the lessor’s consent per CIMBT’s standard process, 
and the legal comment for the case that lessor shall not provide consent are as followed; 
“CIMBT’s standard process for BSA over land lease agreement requires the consent from the lessor on the following purposes; 
(i) the lessor will not amend the lease without the bank’s knowledge; 
(ii) the lessor will inform the bank prior to the sale or dispose of assets; 
(iii) the lessor will not terminate the lease until the bank’s consent is given; and 
(iv) if BSA is enforced, the lessor will enable purchaser of lease rights to step in as lessee under the land lease. 
Whilst the bank can register BSA without the lessor’s consent, the bank will lose certain rights in (i) to (iv) above but perhaps the most 
concern is rights in no. (i) and (iii) because the buildings we financed (and is mortgages to the bank) is standing on the lease for which 
the bank does not have a certainty that the lessor will not terminate or amend the lease without prior notice to the bank."

Could you summarize this?
The University of the Philippines (UP/we), which includes relevant UP System administration and Constituent University (CU) offices, will make use of fully automated means to process the personal information and sensitive personal information (personal data) contained in the application that your child/dependent/ward will submit through the University of the Philippines College Admission Test (UPCAT) portal (https://upcat2025online.up.edu.ph/) to determine whether or not he/she is eligible to enroll in UP as a first year student for an undergraduate course. We use such automated means as the sole basis in deciding thousands of UPCAT applications as well as any appeals made thereon that we receive in order to efficiently process the same, prevent human error or bias and enable us to treat applicants fairly.

Section 18 (c) of the Memo Circular 2023-04 of the National Privacy Commission states:

A PIC shall obtain the consent of the data subject when automated processing is the sole basis for a decision that produces legal effects on or may significantly affect the data subject.

Since we wish to comply with the Philippine Data Privacy Act (PDPA) and uphold you and your child/dependent/ward's data privacy rights, we therefore request you and your child/dependent/ward to carefully read and thereafter indicate your consent for us to process the personal data of your child/dependent/ward as well as your personal data, by submitting this certification and data privacy consent form through electronic means via the UPCAT portal should you wish your child/dependent/ward to proceed with his or her UPCAT application.

If you do not grant consent, or thereafter withdraw your consent, we regret that we will not be able to process the UPCAT application as well as any appeals thereon of your child/dependent/ward.

While we obtain your consent for such automated decision-making means, please note that our processing of your personal data in your application and any appeal thereon as well as supporting documents that you submit is ultimately based on UPs right to exercise academic freedom under the 1987 Constitution, our Charter R.A. 9500, other applicable laws such as the Education Act of 1982 and Philippine jurisprudence. The right to academic freedom includes the right of UP to determine who may be admitted to study in UP. You may wish to refer to the case of Garcia vs. Faculty Admissions Committee Loyola School of Theology G.R. No. L-40779 November 28, 1975 68 SCRA 277 (1975) cited in University of the Philippines vs. Arokiaswamy G.R. No. 134625. August 31, 1999 https://elibrary.judiciary.gov.ph/thebookshelf/showdocs/1/36888 which states:

“Wide indeed is the sphere of autonomy granted to institutions of higher learning, for the constitutional grant of academic freedom, to quote again from Garcia v. Faculty Admission Committee, Loyola School of Theology, "is not to be construed in a niggardly manner or in a grudging fashion."

Academic freedom: “is a freedom granted to "institutions of higher learning" which is thus given "a wide sphere of authority certainly extending to the choice of students."

I certify that:

(1) all the information which my child/dependent/ward provided in support of his/her application, which includes appeals thereon, are true, complete and accurate.

(2) I read all information contained in the General Information Bulletin on First Year Admissions for Academic Year 2025-2026 and agree to abide by UP's rules, including those on admission, processing fees, tuition, scholarships and financial assistance programs.

(3) I read and understood the UP System Privacy Notice for First Year Admissions for Academic Year 2025-2026.

(4) I am aware that my child/dependent/ward's application shall be subject to – among others – Republic Act No. 10533 (or the K-12 Law), its implementing rules and regulations, and all relevant Department of Education issuances.

(5) I recognize that in signing this application form, I share with my child/dependent/ward the responsibility for the veracity and completeness of the information supplied.

I grant my consent to the University of the Philippines to process my personal data and that of my child/dependent/ward pursuant to Sec. 18 (c) of the National Privacy Commission Memorandum Circular 2023-04 listed below, including:

(1) my name;

(2) my citizenship;

(3) my civil status;

(4) my highest educational attainment;

(5) my occupation, employer, and annual income or annual pension;

(6) my signature;

(7) my child/dependent/ward's name;

(8) my child/dependent/ward's photograph with nameplate and signature;;

(9) my child/dependent/ward's signature;

(10) my child/dependent/ward's date and place of birth;

(11) my child/dependent/ward's citizenship;

(12) the information in my child/dependent/ward's Philippine passport or Bureau of Immigration identification certificate (if applicable);

(13) my child/dependent/ward's contact information;

(14) my child/dependent/ward's registered email address, and access credentials;

(15) my child/dependent/ward's educational records, information regarding my child/dependent/ward's education including his or her learner reference number (if any), and UPCAT scores;

(16) my child/dependent/ward's choice of UPCAT test center;

(17) my child/dependent/ward's choice of campuses and programs;

(18) whether my child/dependent/ward is a member of an indigenous people's group (i.e., indigenous cultural community), and the information contained in the certification issued by the National Commission on Indigenous Peoples or the National Commission on Muslim Filipinos that he or she submitted;

(19) whether my child/dependent/ward has any physical disability or medical condition that will make it difficult for him or her to take a regular test, and the corresponding medical certificate;

(20) the citizenship, civil status, highest educational attainment, occupation, employer (including whether the applicant is a child of a UP faculty member or employee), gross annual income or pension of the father, mother or legal guardian (other than parents) of my child/dependent/ward and estimated gross annual income of my child/dependent/ward's household;

(21) the number of other household members and other relatives providing support for the upkeep of the household of my child/dependent/ward, and the respective contributions of such other persons, demographic and socio-economic information about my child/dependent/ward, my child/dependent/ward's parents or guardians, as well as our household and his or her answers to questions regarding whether s/he thinks s/he may need financial and other assistance in the event s/he is deemed eligible to enroll in UP; and

(22) information contained in the school ID or any valid government issued ID (GIID) card of my child/dependent/ward and my GIID (in the event I will be providing a copy of the same);

for processing the application of my child/dependent/ward to be admitted as a first year student for an undergraduate course in UP through fully automated decision-making means via the UPCAT portal including, but not limited to all other related purposes:

(a) verifying my identity;

(b) preventing fraud;

(c) documenting consent for the processing of my personal data for such UPCAT application and;

(d) contacting me regarding my child/dependent/ward's application;

(e) determining whether my child/dependent/ward is required to pay a processing fee;

I further agree that, if my child/dependent/ward was permitted by UP to submit a paper-based application that UP, through the Ugnayan ng Pahinungod unit that collected the paper-based application or UPCAT examiner will likewise provide my child/dependent/ward with the print out of his or her UPCAT test permit after he or she shows such unit personnel or the UPCAT examiner his or her valid school ID or GIID. As stated below, my child/dependent/ward and I understand that all UP personnel as well as any Pahinungod volunteer that processes our personal data are required to execute the proper non-disclosure undertaking in order to uphold our right to data privacy. I likewise understand and agree that UP through its duly authorized personnel is authorized to encode and double check my personal data and that of my child/dependent/ward for the purpose of enabling the University to process such application through fully automated decision-making means.

I further certify that I obtained consent from all third persons, whose personal data are provided in support of my child/ward/dependent's application, to allow UP to process such information as explained in the abovementioned privacy notice and in this certification and consent form, and agree to hold UP free and harmless from all liabilities in connection with the processing of the personal data of such third persons.

I understand that as stated in the abovementioned privacy notice for UPCAT that UP is authorized to process my personal data as well as that of my child/dependent/ward for other lawful purposes as provided under the PDPA and other applicable laws including research, processing for the purpose of exercising its right and responsibility of academic freedom, compliance with legal obligations and issuances of public authorities which may include disclosure of my personal data to such public authorities, for the purpose of establishing or defending legal claims and defenses, etc. and that therefore UP will continue to securely store my personal data for as long as necessary in order to fulfill such other legitimate purposes as allowed by the PDPA and other applicable laws.

I am aware that the processing of personal data for the UPCAT application and any appeal thereon of my child/dependent/ward carries risks that may involve the confidentiality, integrity and availability of personal data or the risk that processing will violate the privacy principles and rights of data subjects. I understand that UP has put in place reasonable physical (e.g. access control measures such as locks, security personnel etc.) organizational (e.g. only authorised personnel who have signed the required non-disclosure undertaking and need such personal data to perform their functions are allowed to process such personal data, privacy impact assessments etc) and technical measures (use of CDN, encryption, multifactor authentication, the conduct of vulnerability and penetration testing and other similar measures) to prevent or mitigate such risks as stated in the abovementioned privacy notice. I understand that such measures do not guarantee absolute protection against such risks as when systems are subject to targeted cyberattacks, malware, ransomware, computer viruses, etc. However, UP has also adopted measures in order to deal with security incidents or personal data breaches in compliance with the PDPA and NPC issuances (Part 7 Security Incident or Breach Response Procedures of the UP System Data Privacy Manual approved by the Board of Regents CERTIFIED TRUE COPY_DATA PRIVACY MANUAL 2023 EDITION.pdf (up.edu.ph) and the corresponding forms for security incident or data breach management UNIVERSITY OF THE PHILIPPINES SYSTEM ADMINISTRATION INCIDENT OR BREACH REPORT FORM.docx (up.edu.ph); PRELIMINARY ASSESSMENT FORM FOR SECURITY INCIDENTS OR PERSONAL DATA BREACHES (up.edu.ph); Mandatory Notification to NPC.pdf (up.edu.ph); Mandatory Personal Data Breach Notification for Data Subjects.docx (up.edu.ph) and SECURITY INCIDENT OR PERSONAL DATA BREACH REPORT (up.edu.ph)).

I agree that I will help keep my and my child/dependent/ward's personal data secure by double checking that the email account he or she will be using for the UPCAT portal has not been compromised by using Have I Been Pwned, using a strong password for such account https://itdc.up.edu.ph/about/advisories/2023%2012%2004%20REMINDER%20-%20Use%20Strong%20Passwords%20for%20UP%20Mail%20Accounts.pdf, when possible activating two-factor authentication for the same, not using public, unsecured networks for submitting personal data or at least using VPN if he or she uses such unsecured networks and keeping his or her UPCAT portal account credentials confidential.

